2	// Staged bundle calibration (CLAUDE.md Stage 3): decompose the curve dependency graph and solve only
3	// what must be solved jointly. Curve c (an instrument's forecast leg) DEPENDS on the other curves that
4	// instrument references (benchmark / discount). Condense into strongly-connected components (Tarjan):
5	//   - a singleton SCC (a curve whose dependencies are already solved) -> a LOCAL LM over just its block,
6	//     with the earlier curves FROZEN as constants;
7	//   - a multi-curve SCC (a genuine cycle of mutual dependence)        -> a joint LM over just those.
8	// SCCs are solved in dependency-first order. On a triangular chain (SOFR->FF->PRIME->PRIME2) every SCC
9	// is a singleton, so it is four small local solves -- like-for-like with QuantLib's sequential bootstrap
10	// -- and no 28-knot global solve. A cycle forces exactly (and only) its members into a joint solve.
11	//
12	// Freezing a solved curve is free: the multi-curve kernel is templated per curve argument, and a frozen
13	// curve enters as a constant (Scalar(value), zero gradient), so the block's AAD Jacobian is the small
14	// per-block one automatically -- no kernel change.
15	
16	#include <Eigen/Core>
17	
18	#include <functional>
19	#include <memory>
20	#include <vector>
